<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48041" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">teucrĭon</span></b> , ĭi,
			n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεύκριον.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>, <i>the germander</i>:
			Teucrium chamaedrys, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 24,
				15, 80, § 130</span></i> (al.
			Teucria).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The herb spleenwort</i>: Teucrium flavium, Linn.;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				25, 5, 20, § 45</span></i>.—Called also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">teucrĭa</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 26, 7,
				19, § 35</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
